        "content": "<p>andrewl6097 opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14752\">issue #14752</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h4>Feature</h4>\n<p><code>GuestProfiler::new</code> demangles every defined function's name and builds a fresh<br>\nsymbol table for each module it is given, every time it is called. The table<br>\ndepends only on the module, so it could be built once per <code>Module</code> and shared by<br>\nevery later profiler.</p>\n<h4>Benefit</h4>\n<p><code>GuestProfiler</code> is documented as suitable for profiling individual guests in a<br>\nmulti-tenant embedder, which suggests one profiler per request. Today each of<br>\nthose profilers pays a setup cost that grows with the size of the module, and<br>\nfor large Rust modules it becomes a large share of the request:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>On a 1.7 MB Rust module with about 1,500 defined functions, <code>new()</code> takes about<br>\n  2.4 ms (measured on wasmtime 43). Demangling the names takes about 2.1 ms of that, and everything in<br>\n<code>new()</code> that does not depend on the module takes under 1 µs. The guest<br>\n  invocation we were profiling ran for about 44 ms, so setup cost more than<br>\n  sampling every millisecond for the whole invocation (about 0.2 ms).  And this was a pathological case; many of our guests run for far shorter time periods so this overhead would be even more painful.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The program below generates modules with N Rust-mangled function names and<br>\n  times <code>new()</code>. On wasmtime 49.0.3, x86_64 Linux, release build:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Functions</th>\n<th><code>GuestProfiler::new</code>, median of 1000</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1,500</td>\n<td>681 µs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10,000</td>\n<td>4.64 ms</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>(The generated names are shorter than real rustc output, which is why the<br>\n1,500-function case is cheaper here than in the real module above.)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt;Reproduction&lt;/summary&gt;</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\"># Cargo.toml</span>\n<span class=\"k\">[package]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"guest-profiler-new-cost\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">version</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"0.0.0\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">edition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"2024\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">publish</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[dependencies]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"49\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">// src/main.rs</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">//! Times `GuestProfiler::new` on a module with many Rust-mangled function names.</span>\n<span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">std</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">fmt</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Write</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">std</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"p\">::{</span><span class=\"n\">Duration</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Instant</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"p\">::{</span><span class=\"n\">Engine</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GuestProfiler</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"nb\">Result</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">funcs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">usize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">std</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">nth</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"n\">map_or</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1500</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parse</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">unwrap</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// Legacy-mangled names shaped like rustc output: crate::module_N::function_N::{hash}.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">String</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">from</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"(module</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"n\">funcs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"fm\">format!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"module_{i}\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"fm\">format!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"function_{i}\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"fm\">writeln!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"s\">\"  (func $_ZN10some_crate{}{}{}{}17h{:016x}E)\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mh\">0x9e37_79b9_7f4a_7c15</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sc\">')'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">engine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Engine</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">engine</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">GuestProfiler</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">engine</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"s\">\"bench\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">Duration</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">from_millis</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">[(</span><span class=\"s\">\"bench.wasm\"</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to_string</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">clone</span><span class=\"p\">())],</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unwrap</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Instant</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nb\">drop</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elapsed</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">times</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Vec</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Duration</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"mi\">1000</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Instant</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"nb\">drop</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elapsed</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">collect</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">times</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sort</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"fm\">println!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s\">\"{funcs} functions: first new() {first:?}, later new() median {:?}, p99 {:?}\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">times</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">500</span><span class=\"p\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">times</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">990</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nb\">Ok</span><span class=\"p\">(())</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run with <code>cargo run --release -- 1500</code> and <code>cargo run --release -- 10000</code>.</p>\n<p>&lt;/details&gt;</p>\n<h4>Implementation</h4>\n<p>Cache the table on the module: a <code>OnceLock&lt;Option&lt;Arc&lt;SymbolTable&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> on<br>\n<code>ModuleInner</code>, behind the <code>profiling</code> feature, filled by <code>module_symbols</code> the<br>\nfirst time a profiler includes the module. <code>fxprof_processed_profile</code> already<br>\nholds a library's symbol table as an <code>Arc&lt;SymbolTable&gt;</code>, so sharing it needs no<br>\ncopy.</p>\n<p>One detail: <code>Profile::add_lib</code> keys libraries by value, so a <code>LibraryInfo</code><br>\ncarrying the table hashes every symbol name on each call. Adding the library<br>\nwithout a table and then attaching the shared table with<br>\n<code>Profile::set_lib_symbol_table</code> avoids that. In my measurements, passing the<br>\ntable inside <code>LibraryInfo</code> made each cached <code>new()</code> on the 1,500-function<br>\nmodule take 31.7 µs, against 16.3 µs with <code>set_lib_symbol_table</code>.</p>\n<p>I have a patch for this and can open a PR.</p>\n<h4>Alternatives</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Hold the table in a separate, reusable profiler object.</strong> This is close to<br>\n  the \"standalone profiler struct where you acquire thread-specific profilers\"<br>\n  idea from the review of #6282. It would mean new public API, while caching on<br>\n<code>Module</code> changes none.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Pass a prebuilt symbol table into <code>GuestProfiler::new</code>.</strong> This also needs<br>\n  new public API, and the embedder would have to keep the table alongside each<br>\n  module.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Have the embedder demangle names at build time.</strong> Rewriting the name<br>\n  section with already-demangled names cuts our 2.4 ms to about 0.65 ms,<br>\n  because both demanglers then fail fast. It needs a build step in every guest<br>\n  toolchain and still costs time on every profile.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Memory cost: the cache keeps one symbol table alive per profiled <code>Module</code> for<br>\nthe module's lifetime. That is roughly the size of the demangled names, about<br>\n240 KB of strings for the 1,500-function module. Modules that are never<br>\nprofiled pay nothing beyond an empty <code>OnceLock</code>.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
